iv data-rid="314356a7-b0e1-4101-aa91-8b0250fa2a4e" class="r-jymq4w" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="open" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="87835d23-baac-4721-9731-e6a335252d7e" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="replo-:R6mr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1mdg13g r-m5qt6b"><div data-rid="c2889f1a-0248-47cc-93ae-58e007c1d938" class="r-1f75dux alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>What are the Tuttle Twins books about?</p></span></div><div data-rid="ac72531f-7772-4366-b424-580d0759ae7b" class="r-129727z" aria-hidden="true"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-b6fa8o" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M4 8a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5h7a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-7A.5.5 0 0 1 4 8"></path></svg></div></div><div class="replo-animated" id="replo-:R6mr2:"><div data-rid="6b3e6d6d-758e-458f-b36f-115b5e4b30c2" class="r-1ffcf54"><div data-rid="acf1e955-2d6c-478f-b429-0c63d1873141" class="r-cv9x2u alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span>The Tuttle Twins books teach kids about timeless principles—like freedom, critical thinking, and personal responsibility—through engaging, age-appropriate stories. Instead of memorizing facts, children discover these ideas by following fun adventures, relatable characters, and real-world examples.</span></p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="f8e9e805-ce1a-421c-af4f-68a1b8a702bb" class="r-15e9dvg" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="f06809dd-048c-4643-8c2f-93ffdc6e23ed" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:Ramr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-14pft8r"><div data-rid="6f46a259-e0c2-4f7d-ae6a-2914983cb9a4" class="r-1s0lxkf alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>What ages are the books for?</p></span></div><div data-rid="79af74bf-39e9-486a-a100-93bc3a9bdc5f" class="r-uzfore" aria-hidden="true"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-s3ugng" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M8 4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v3h3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-3v3a.5.5 0 0 1-1 0v-3h-3a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1h3v-3A.5.5 0 0 1 8 4"></path></svg></div></div><div class="replo-animated" hidden="" id="replo-:Ramr2:"><div data-rid="9eda969e-e62d-411c-9694-063e245fab14" class="r-1h57pj7"><div data-rid="214f881a-857d-48a3-a2c0-0e863abfef79" class="r-1f2yu2x alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>We have books for every stage of your child’s development:</p><p><strong>Ages 0–4:</strong> Board books with colorful illustrations and simple ideas.</p><p><strong>Ages 5–7:</strong> Picture books with short, engaging stories.</p><p><strong>Ages 8–12:</strong> Chapter books that explore deeper concepts.</p><p><strong>Ages 13+:</strong> Teen and young adult books with more advanced discussions.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="97369ca7-36af-425f-aaa6-08bb01112e9f" class="r-1dduido" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="bac2b6fb-f670-412c-bab6-5b4d82b8b3d5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:Remr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-18cjx8q"><div data-rid="5d4d491a-7aed-4838-b0ab-ad8f1160d170" class="r-ibqato alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Do my kids need any prior knowledge to understand these books?</p></span></div><div data-rid="8bf84c30-42d3-40c3-b983-ce577c35cc92" class="r-1re7csy" aria-hidden="true"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-6wdp35" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M8 4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v3h3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-3v3a.5.5 0 0 1-1 0v-3h-3a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1h3v-3A.5.5 0 0 1 8 4"></path></svg></div></div><div class="replo-animated" hidden="" id="replo-:Remr2:"><div data-rid="3681fef8-66fa-471d-b732-c64951890030" class="r-173fnni"><div data-rid="40b4b8c5-096a-4861-8aab-b39e4307f1f3" class="r-r13fl1 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span>Not at all! Each story starts from scratch, making it easy for any child to understand—whether they’ve heard of these ideas before or not. The books are written to make learning feel like play, so kids naturally remember what they’ve learned.</span></p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="3d0311ae-ca13-4b2f-b843-6f94c33c2ec5" class="r-11nkbfv" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="da406afe-83c3-45b1-b160-368e0b90dece" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:Rimr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-w292rc"><div data-rid="b0dc500e-8d63-412a-8f22-b640f8463643" class="r-laurz4 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>How do these books compare to school textbooks?</p></span></div><div data-rid="d4c4a413-d341-4705-9295-14c766712533" class="r-psjq4" aria-hidden="true"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-k6zmgo" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M8 4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v3h3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-3v3a.5.5 0 0 1-1 0v-3h-3a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1h3v-3A.5.5 0 0 1 8 4"></path></svg></div></div><div class="replo-animated" hidden="" id="replo-:Rimr2:"><div data-rid="e06b99d3-b00d-4312-9d31-a2c184a5f602" class="r-a7tyuz"><div data-rid="291f145a-f37c-4f52-b677-a08259e830c9" class="r-1bnftv alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span>Unlike most textbooks, the Tuttle Twins use storytelling to make learning effortless and memorable. Research shows kids recall and understand more when lessons are woven into an engaging story rather than presented as dry facts.</span></p></span></div></div></div></div